      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{642b3036ffd38909cda88cd4|full_name} It is of course better with the @everyone role, but \n\nFor my group, as an example, I would like to have the following\n\n1 - Owner role \n\n2 - Admin (Has all perms)\n\n3 - Moderator (Has lots of moderation perms)\n\n4 - Trusted (Has some instance moderation perms and Manage Invites for example)\n\n5 - Ranked Host (Very similar to Trusted with just few things on top) eg. Has Manage Group Instances on top of what Trusted has\n\n6 - Host (Has only Manage Instance perm)\n\nSo, for me personally, I'm only missing 2 management roles but I've seen some other people require ~8 or so, of course, another question is if these people could possibly deduplicate their roles because there's likely gonna be some overlap but in either case, it would likely give a lot more freedom if we had 10 (9) management roles limit.\n\nAlso, another possibility is to make Owner's role not count as management",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
